---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import SupportEmail from '../../components/SupportEmail.astro';

const title = 'Terms of Use — Keyboard Studio';
const description =
  'Terms of Use for Keyboard Studio, including paid download terms, permitted use, local data responsibility, and disclaimers.';
const effectiveDate = 'July 28, 2026';
const lastUpdated = 'August 13, 2026';
---

<PageLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/terms/">
  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h1>Keyboard Studio Terms of Use</h1>
      <p>
        These Terms of Use govern your use of Keyboard Studio for iPhone and iPad.
        They are provided by the developer of Keyboard Studio. This page is not
        legal advice.
      </p>
      <div class="meta-row">
        <span>Effective Date: {effectiveDate}</span>
        <span>Last Updated: {lastUpdated}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container container--narrow prose" style="padding-bottom: 4rem;">
    <nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="toc-heading">
      <p class="toc__title" id="toc-heading">On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#acceptance">Acceptance</a></li>
        <li><a href="#paid-download">Paid App Store download</a></li>
        <li><a href="#no-subscriptions">No subscriptions or In-App Purchases</a></li>
        <li><a href="#permitted-use">Permitted use</a></li>
        <li><a href="#user-content">User-created content</a></li>
        <li><a href="#local-data">Local data responsibility</a></li>
        <li><a href="#data-loss">No guarantee against data loss</a></li>
        <li><a href="#updates">Software updates</a></li>
        <li><a href="#notices">Third-party and open-source notices</a></li>
        <li><a href="#esdb">ESDB attribution reference</a></li>
        <li><a href="#apple-eula">Apple standard EULA relationship</a></li>
        <li><a href="#disclaimer">Disclaimer</a></li>
        <li><a href="#liability">Limitation of liability</a></li>
        <li><a href="#termination">Termination</a></li>
        <li><a href="#changes">Changes</a></li>
        <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="acceptance">Acceptance</h2>
    <p>
      By downloading, installing, or using Keyboard Studio, you agree to these
      Terms of Use. If you do not agree, do not use Keyboard Studio.
    </p>

    <h2 id="paid-download">Paid App Store download</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio is planned as a paid App Store download for iPhone and iPad.
      Purchase and distribution are handled through Apple’s App Store under Apple’s
      applicable terms.
    </p>

    <h2 id="no-subscriptions">No subscriptions or In-App Purchases</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio is intended as a pay-once download. There are no
      subscriptions, feature tiers, consumable purchases, Restore Purchase flow, or
      advertisements offered by Keyboard Studio. All included features are available
      after installation.
    </p>

    <h2 id="permitted-use">Permitted use</h2>
    <p>
      You may use Keyboard Studio for personal or lawful purposes on devices you
      own or control, in accordance with these Terms, Apple’s App Store terms, and
      applicable law. You may not reverse engineer, redistribute, or misuse the
      software except where such restriction is prohibited by law.
    </p>

    <h2 id="user-content">User-created content</h2>
    <p>
      You are responsible for Quick Phrases, Personal Dictionary entries, custom
      themes, user-selected Photo Backgrounds, and other content you create or
      select in Keyboard Studio. Do not store or select content that you are not
      permitted to keep or use on your device.
    </p>

    <h2 id="local-data">Local data responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio stores settings, phrases, dictionary entries, processed Photo
      Backgrounds, and related preferences locally on your device. When Full Access
      is enabled, supported data may be shared locally between the App and Keyboard
      Extension through an App Group container. This is not a cloud backup service.
      You are responsible for managing content you create or select.
    </p>

    <h2 id="data-loss">No guarantee against data loss</h2>
    <p>
      The developer of Keyboard Studio does not guarantee that local data will
      never be lost. Device failure, operating-system behavior, App deletion,
      backups, restores, and user actions can affect locally stored data. Keyboard
      Studio does not promise cloud recovery of deleted local data. Maintain your
      own backups where important and permitted by the relevant feature.
    </p>

    <h2 id="updates">Software updates</h2>
    <p>
      The developer may provide updates that change features, fix issues, or
      improve compatibility. Updates are delivered through the App Store when
      available. Continued use after an update is subject to these Terms and any
      updated terms published on this website.
    </p>

    <h2 id="notices">Third-party and open-source notices</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio may include third-party or open-source components. Notices
      and licenses for those components are provided as required, including within
      the App where applicable.
    </p>

    <h2 id="esdb">ESDB attribution reference</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio uses the English Speller Database (ESDB), formerly SCOWL, as
      a bundled offline lexicon. Keyboard Studio does not claim ownership of ESDB.
      Concise attribution is provided here; full license and attribution are
      available offline inside the Keyboard Studio App.
    </p>

    <h2 id="apple-eula">Apple standard EULA relationship</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent Keyboard Studio is distributed through the App Store, Apple’s
      Licensed Application End User License Agreement (or the Apple standard EULA
      then in effect) may also apply. If there is a conflict between these Terms and
      Apple’s required terms for App Store distribution, Apple’s required terms
      control for that conflict to the extent required by Apple.
    </p>

    <h2 id="disclaimer">Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio is provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of
      any kind, whether express or implied, including implied warranties of
      merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement, to
      the maximum extent permitted by law. The developer of Keyboard Studio does
      not warrant uninterrupted or error-free operation.
    </p>

    <h2 id="liability">Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, the developer of Keyboard Studio is
      not liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive
      damages, or for any loss of data, profits, or business, arising out of or
      related to your use of Keyboard Studio. Some jurisdictions do not allow
      certain limitations; in those jurisdictions, liability is limited to the
      fullest extent permitted.
    </p>

    <h2 id="termination">Termination</h2>
    <p>
      Your right to use Keyboard Studio ends if you violate these Terms or if you
      delete the App. Provisions that by their nature should survive termination,
      including disclaimers and limitations of liability, will survive.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms may be updated from time to time. The Last Updated date at the
      top of this page will change when updates are published. You should review
      the Terms periodically.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For legal and product inquiries about these Terms, contact the developer of
      Keyboard Studio at <SupportEmail subject="Keyboard Studio Terms" />.
    </p>
    <p>
      These Terms are not legal advice and do not create an attorney-client
      relationship.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
